    2. Design the legend pattern in lattice coords (3-4 rows x 2-3 cols, 6-10 filled positions, 2-4 colors, staircase shape).
    3. Choose base offset (base_r, base_c) for the block area such that all legend-mapped blocks fit in grid AND the block area columns don't overlap with legend pixel columns (base_c >= 8).
    4. Place all NxN blocks on the grid per legend mapping (this is the output).
    5. Pick one legend row with >=2 filled positions; pick 2 adjacent filled positions from it as the input blocks. Verify the 2 blocks yield a unique base offset via solver voting.
    6. Remove all blocks except the 2 chosen ones to get the input. Legend pixels remain.
