generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build clean output structure, then inject spurs/ noise to get input)
  steps:
    - Pick grid size H,W in [16,19].
    - Partition the grid into 2-5 large rectangular/L-shaped regions with random axis-aligned cuts; assign alternating colors (blue=1, black=0) so adjacent regions differ. Enforce each region bbox fill >= 0.5 and region size >= ~30.
    - For each large black region, optionally add 0-2 leaf protrusions that extend into an adjacent blue region as a short 1-2 cell stub (leaf pixel has <=1 black 4-neighbor inside the original region).
